-- title:
--   Theorem 3.11 — $(W,\Psi)\cong(W,\mathbb E(\Psi\mid\mathcal F_W))$; every coloured graphon is equivalent to a simply coloured one
-- statement:
--   Let $(W,\Psi)$ be a $\kappa$-coloured graphon on $[0,1]$ with Lebesgue measure, and let
--   $$
--   \bar\Psi=(\bar\psi_i)_{i=1}^\kappa:=\mathbb E(\Psi\mid\mathcal F_W)
--   $$
--   be the conditional expectation of $\Psi$, coordinatewise, with respect to the σ-field $\mathcal F_W$ generated by the sections $x\mapsto W_x$, in a version with values in $\Delta_\kappa$. Then
--   $$
--   (W,\Psi)\cong(W,\bar\Psi).
--   $$
--   Consequently, every coloured graphon on $[0,1]$ is equivalent to some simply coloured graphon on $[0,1]$.
--
--   Simply coloured graphons are the class for which the uniqueness theorem 3.14 holds, so this reduction is what makes that theorem apply to every coloured graph limit.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathbb E(\Psi\mid\mathcal F_W)$ is determined only up to a null set. The first clause is stated for every colouring $\bar\Psi$ that is $\mathcal F_W$-measurable and whose coordinates are a.e. equal to Mathlib's conditional expectations `volume[ψ_i | sigmaW W]`; the second clause asserts the existence of a simply coloured $(W',\Psi')$ on $[0,1]$ equivalent to $(W,\Psi)$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: Ψ̄ := E(Ψ | F_W), a version with values in Δκ → every colouring Ψ̄ that is F_W-measurable and coordinatewise a.e. equal to condExp (sigmaW W) ψ_i; reason: the conditional expectation is defined up to null sets; the statement covers every Δκ-valued F_W-measurable version
--   - encoding: F_W: σ-field generated by x ↦ W_x ∈ L¹[0, 1] (Borel) → sigmaW W: comap of the Borel σ-field of Lp ℝ 1 under sectionL1 W; reason: the same σ-field; the fallback value of sectionL1 is never used for graphons
--   - encoding: [0, 1] with Lebesgue measure λ → unitInterval with volume and the Borel σ-field; reason: Remark 3.3: the Borel and Lebesgue σ-fields give the same results up to a.e. equality
--   - encoding: W₁ ≅ W₂ (Definition 2.6: one, and thus all, of the conditions of Lemma 2.5) → CEquiv: t(F, W₁) = t(F, W₂) for every coloured graph F; reason: condition (i) of Lemma 2.5, which Definition 2.6 lists as equivalent to the others
--   - encoding: colourings Ψ : Ω → Δκ, colours [κ]; pure colourings χ : Ω → [κ] → Ψ : Ω → Fin κ → ℝ with measurable nonnegative coordinates summing to 1 (IsKColouring); pure χ measurable with the point-mass colouring ofColour χ; reason: the same objects (Definition 2.1, p.7), with colours numbered 0, …, κ − 1
-- source:
--   Janson, Lo, McDiarmid, Skeja, Skerman, Graphon Colourings and Limits of Graph Partitions, arXiv:2610.38599 (held version, sha256 3d198813a65d248922299a3380e10f238dbc5dcd3be060f7810b462bd5d3d10f), Theorem 3.11, p.23 (PDF p.23)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GraphonCheeger_Supplement_homDens
import Definitions.Def_GraphonCheeger_Supplement_sigmaW

open MeasureTheory

namespace GraphonCheeger.Supplement

/-- Theorem 3.11, p.23 (Janson, Lo, McDiarmid, Skeja, Skerman, *Graphon Colourings and Limits of Graph Partitions*,
arXiv:2610.38599 (held version, sha256 3d198813…)): let `(W, Ψ)` be a coloured graphon on `[0, 1]` and define a new colouring
`Ψ̄ = (ψ̄_i)_{i=1}^κ := E(Ψ | F_W)` (3.47). Then `(W, Ψ) ≅ (W, Ψ̄)`. Consequently, every coloured graphon
is equivalent to some simply coloured graphon.

**Formalization Note.**
* §3.2.2 considers only graphons on `[0, 1]` with Lebesgue measure (`volume` on `unitInterval`).
* `E(Ψ | F_W)` is defined only up to a null set, and is taken coordinatewise in a version with
  values in `Δ_κ` (p.23). The first clause holds for every such version: every colouring `Ψ̄`
  (measurable into `Δ_κ`) that is `F_W`-measurable (`IsSimpleColouring`) and whose coordinates are
  a.e. equal to Mathlib's conditional expectations `E(ψ_i | F_W)` (`condExp` w.r.t. `sigmaW W`).
* The second clause: some simply coloured graphon `(W', Ψ')` on `[0, 1]` is equivalent to
  `(W, Ψ)`. -/
theorem theorem_3_11 {κ : ℕ} (W : unitInterval → unitInterval → ℝ) (hW : IsGraphon W)
    (Ψ : unitInterval → Fin κ → ℝ) (hΨ : IsKColouring Ψ) :
    (∀ Ψbar : unitInterval → Fin κ → ℝ, IsKColouring Ψbar → IsSimpleColouring W Ψbar →
      (∀ i, (fun x => Ψbar x i) =ᵐ[volume] (volume[fun x => Ψ x i | sigmaW W])) →
      CEquiv volume W Ψ volume W Ψbar) ∧
    ∃ (W' : unitInterval → unitInterval → ℝ) (Ψ' : unitInterval → Fin κ → ℝ),
      IsGraphon W' ∧ IsKColouring Ψ' ∧ IsSimpleColouring W' Ψ' ∧
      CEquiv volume W Ψ volume W' Ψ' := by sorry

end GraphonCheeger.Supplement
